{0 Getting started}

This guide gets one Lwt-Unix program from installation to its first point and
wide logs.

{1 Install}

Install the ready runtime package:

{[
opam install observe-lwt-unix
]}

Add the libraries and optional PPX to the executable:

{[
(executable
 (name main)
 (libraries observe observe-lwt-unix lwt.unix)
 (preprocess
  (pps observe.ppx)))
]}

{1 Initialize once}

{[
let config =
  Observe.Config.create_exn ~service:"orders"
    ~environment:"development" ()

let () = Observe_lwt_unix.init_exn config
]}

[service] is the only required configuration value. With everything else
omitted, Observe:

- admits [Info], [Warn], and [Error];
- chooses pretty output for an absent, [dev], or [development] environment and
  NDJSON otherwise;
- applies finite canonical-materialization defaults;
- installs no caller-defined enrichment or redaction;
- performs no sampling; and
- adds no filesystem output.

Use {!val:Observe.Config.create} when initialization errors belong in an
explicit result. [create_exn] raises a typed
{!exception:Observe.Config.Invalid_configuration} at the composition root.

{1 Log}

{[
[%observe.info text ~tag:"startup" "service ready"];

[%observe.info
  untyped { action = "order_created"; order_id = "ord-42"; items = 3 }]
]}

Point authoring is admission-first: if no active route accepts the selected
level, the author callback and its formatting arguments do not run.

{1 Run an operation}

{[
let checkout () =
  let log = Observe.Logs.current () in
  [%observe.set log { cart_id = "cart-42"; phase = "started" }];
  authorize_payment ()

let app () =
  Observe_lwt_unix.with_operation ~name:"checkout" checkout
]}

[with_operation] creates a wide event, binds it as current, and makes one final
publication attempt when the callback returns, raises, or is cancelled. An
ordinary escaping exception is interpreted into the wide event and then
re-raised with its original backtrace. If error interpretation or final
materialization fails, Observe withholds the operation and reports the failure.
Cancellation and other runtime control exceptions complete without inferred
error meaning and remain native. The default interpreter is
{!val:Observe.Error.exn}; pass [~error] when the domain has a richer reusable
interpretation.

{1 Finish output}

{[
let () =
  Observe_lwt_unix.init_exn config;
  Lwt_main.run (Lwt.finalize app Observe_lwt_unix.shutdown)
]}

Console and ready filesystem outputs are asynchronous. Call [shutdown] at the
process composition boundary so accepted work gets a final attempt and owned
workers and resources are released. [flush] is the non-terminal accepted-work
boundary when logging must remain open. See {!page-outputs} for exact claims and
advanced reports.

